---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout title={`${site.name} | ${site.tagline}`} description={site.description}>
  <Header />

  <section class="relative min-h-[100svh] overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute inset-0">
      <img
        src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1553877522-43269d4ea984?auto=format&fit=crop&w=2000&q=80"
        alt="Team reviewing operational workflow and data"
        class="hero-bg absolute inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover"
        width="2000"
        height="1333"
        fetchpriority="high"
      />
      <div class="hero-scrim absolute inset-0"></div>
      <div class="contour-overlay absolute inset-0 opacity-30"></div>
    </div>

    <div
      class="relative z-10 mx-auto flex min-h-[100svh] max-w-6xl items-end px-5 pb-14 pt-28 lg:items-center lg:px-8 lg:pb-24 lg:pt-24"
    >
      <div class="max-w-xl lg:max-w-[38rem]">
        <p
          class="animate-rise font-display text-5xl font-extrabold leading-none tracking-tight text-white sm:text-6xl md:text-7xl"
        >
          {site.name}
        </p>
        <h1
          class="animate-rise-delay-1 mt-6 font-display text-[1.6rem] font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight text-white sm:text-3xl md:text-[2.1rem]"
        >
          We find operational gaps, build custom systems to close them, and turn that data into
          reporting and forecasting you can trust.
        </h1>
        <p class="animate-rise-delay-2 mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-white/82 md:text-lg">
          DSSI is a founder-led software studio—not an off-the-shelf product—that works with any
          organization where day-to-day operations create data worth using.
        </p>
        <div class="animate-rise-delay-3 mt-8 flex w-full flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row">
          <a href={site.primaryCtaHref} class="btn-primary w-full sm:w-auto">{site.primaryCta}</a>
          <a href={site.secondaryCtaHref} class="btn-ghost-hero w-full sm:w-auto">
            {site.secondaryCta}
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Who we are -->
  <section class="bg-surface-elevated">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-20 md:px-8 md:py-24">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink md:text-4xl">Who we are</h2>
      <div class="mt-8 max-w-3xl space-y-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-muted md:text-lg">
        <p>
          DSSI designs and builds <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">custom operational software</strong>
          for teams that have outgrown spreadsheets and email—but do not need another bloated platform.
          We are <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">founder-led</strong>: the people you meet on the
          fit call are the people who map the gap and ship the system.
        </p>
        <p>
          We are honest about where we are today: <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">we have no
          client logos to parade yet</strong>. We are looking for early partners who want a clear build
          path, fixed scope, and software people actually use—not shelfware.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-10 max-w-2xl border-l-2 border-accent pl-4 font-display text-lg font-semibold text-ink">
        Builders first. Your process, your data model, your system.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What we do -->
  <section class="border-t-[3px] border-accent bg-surface">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-20 md:px-8 md:py-24">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight md:text-4xl">What we do</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-base text-ink-muted md:text-lg">
        We do three things in order—only moving ahead when the data is ready.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-14 grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-3 md:divide-x md:divide-border">
        <article class="md:pr-8">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-ink-muted">Step 1</p>
          <h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-xl font-semibold">Discover gaps</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            We interview stakeholders, map how work really flows, and name where time, money, or trust
            leaks—handoffs, duplicate entry, numbers nobody believes.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="md:px-8">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-ink-muted">Step 2</p>
          <h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-xl font-semibold">Build custom systems</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            We ship focused software that bridges the gap: workflows, forms, approvals, integrations,
            and views your team uses daily—not a generic ERP replacement.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="md:pl-8">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-ink-muted">Step 3</p>
          <h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-xl font-semibold">Warehouse, then AI</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            We consolidate operational data into a data warehouse, then add practical AI—ad hoc
            questions, reports, and forecasting—when the data is reliable enough to deserve it.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-10 max-w-2xl text-sm text-ink-muted">
        Most engagements start with one painful process. The full capability is there when you are
        ready to expand.
      </p>
      <a
        href="/audit"
        class="mt-6 inline-flex text-sm font-semibold text-ink underline decoration-accent decoration-2 underline-offset-4 hover:text-hero-mist"
      >
        Start with the Operational Gap Audit →
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Who we serve -->
  <section class="bg-surface-elevated">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-20 md:px-8 md:py-24">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight md:text-4xl">Who we work with</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-muted md:text-lg">
        We work with <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">any industry where operations create
        data</strong>—distribution, professional services, healthcare operations, logistics, light
        manufacturing, agencies with fulfillment, and more. The pattern is the same: volume and
        complexity grew, but the tools between your core system and reality did not.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-10 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
        <li class="border-t-2 border-accent pt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
          <span class="font-medium text-ink">Example:</span> Wholesalers reconciling inventory across
          warehouse and sales
        </li>
        <li class="border-t-2 border-accent pt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
          <span class="font-medium text-ink">Example:</span> Service businesses tracking jobs, parts,
          and billing in one place
        </li>
        <li class="border-t-2 border-accent pt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
          <span class="font-medium text-ink">Example:</span> Operators who need leadership numbers
          faster than “export five spreadsheets”
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-8 max-w-xl text-sm text-ink-muted">
        Strong fit when an owner, COO, or ops lead is tired of asking, “Can someone verify this
        number?”—regardless of sector.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Why DSSI -->
  <section class="bg-surface">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-20 md:px-8 md:py-24">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight md:text-4xl">Why {site.name}</h2>
      <div class="mt-10 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="border-t border-border pt-5">
          <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold">Gap-first, not platform-first</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            We prioritize the operational need and the metric that proves it closed—not a multi-year
            transformation deck.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="border-t border-border pt-5">
          <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold">Custom systems that match how you work</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            Your handoffs, approvals, and integrations—not a forced template sold the same way to
            everyone.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="border-t border-border pt-5">
          <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold">Data and AI with guardrails</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            Warehouse and AI follow trustworthy operations data. Reporting and forecasting you can
            explain in a Monday meeting.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="border-t border-border pt-5">
          <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold">Fixed scope, honest timeline</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            Paid discovery, written pilot scope, milestones. Expand only after daily use.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="bg-surface-elevated">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-20 md:px-8 md:py-24">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight md:text-4xl">FAQ</h2>
      <div class="mt-10 space-y-3">
        <details class="border border-border bg-surface-elevated open:bg-surface">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none px-5 py-4 font-display text-base font-semibold">
            Do you replace our ERP or core accounting system?
          </summary>
          <p class="border-t border-border px-5 py-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            No. We build what sits beside it—the workflows and visibility your core system never
            covered.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details class="border border-border bg-surface-elevated open:bg-surface">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none px-5 py-4 font-display text-base font-semibold">
            What industries do you serve?
          </summary>
          <p class="border-t border-border px-5 py-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            Anywhere operational work generates data we can structure and use. Sector examples show
            patterns—they do not limit who we work with.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details class="border border-border bg-surface-elevated open:bg-surface">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none px-5 py-4 font-display text-base font-semibold">
            Is this an “AI company”?
          </summary>
          <p class="border-t border-border px-5 py-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            We are an operations and custom software company. AI is a layer on clean operational
            data: reports, ad hoc analysis, and forecasting—not a magic box before the process works.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details class="border border-border bg-surface-elevated open:bg-surface">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none px-5 py-4 font-display text-base font-semibold">
            How does AI show up in practice?
          </summary>
          <p class="border-t border-border px-5 py-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            Usually after a custom system and warehouse foundation: questions over your data,
            recurring reports, forward-looking views. Sometimes embedded in the app; sometimes
            through a channel your team already uses—we decide together in scope.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details class="border border-border bg-surface-elevated open:bg-surface">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none px-5 py-4 font-display text-base font-semibold">
            You have no customer logos—why should we trust you?
          </summary>
          <p class="border-t border-border px-5 py-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            Because we would rather show you a written gap brief and a fixed pilot scope than invent
            social proof. Early partners get founder attention and a direct line to delivery.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand
    headline="Ready to name the gap—and see the full path to custom systems and data?"
    body="Book a 30-minute fit call or start with the Operational Gap Audit. Fixed scope. No invented logos."
  />
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
